concern:
  heading: "Your brand voice, and staying on the right side of the law"
  body: >
    <p>Generic AI copy is obvious, and an agency's writing is part of its brand. We spend
    real time on making output sound like your agency specifically, using your existing
    listings as the reference rather than accepting the default register — that is the
    difference between a tool your agents use and one they quietly abandon.</p>
    <p>The second point matters more. Generated property copy will invent a feature, round
    a measurement, or produce a price statement that creates an underquoting or misleading
    conduct problem, and Australian consumer law does not care that a tool wrote it. We
    train the review step as a fixed part of the workflow, with particular attention to
    price, measurements, zoning and anything stated as a fact about the property. Your
    agency finishes with a written policy your principal can stand behind.</p>
